period: 2026-10
entries:
  - venture: donor-retention-analyzer
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built donor-retention-analyzer: a browser-local tool for small
        nonprofits. Paste or upload a gift history (donor, date, amount) and pick the
        fiscal year start; it computes retention by fiscal year (donors who gave in
        two consecutive full years) with a 300-resample seeded bootstrap 80% range,
        first-year versus repeat retention, net dollar retention, new and won-back
        donors, concentration of the top ten donors, and LYBUNT and SYBUNT lists
        ranked by expected dollars: a pooled empirical chance of giving within the
        next 365 days by status and giving-years band (counted at past dates from
        the organisation's own gifts, shrunk toward the overall rate), times the
        median of the donor's last three gifts. A hold-out refits on older dates and
        calls the model unstable when it misses the latest year's donor count by
        more than 25%. Refuses under 30 donors, 60 gifts or two full fiscal years;
        leaves unfinished and mid-year-start years out of every rate. New niche:
        duplicate_check.py best match 0.12 (stripe-churn-cohort-analyzer, a
        subscription tool); nothing in the catalogue serves charities. First visitor
        expected from "how to calculate donor retention rate" and "LYBUNT report"
        searches. Donor data never leaves the browser. Unverified on a real
        organisation: tests use hand-counted retention and dollar retention, a fiscal
        year starting in July, simulated memoryless donors with a known 50% chance
        recovered by the model, a behaviour shift the hold-out must flag, and
        no-network assertions. Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI
        workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: private-practice-payer-mix-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built private-practice-payer-mix-calculator: a browser-local
        tool for therapists and counselors in private practice. Paste one row per
        payer (allowed amount, sessions a month, share of claims paid, days to
        payment, billing minutes); it computes net per session and per clinical hour
        for every insurance panel and the cash fee after denials, billing-service
        fee and admin time, receivables owed, the break-even refill share for
        dropping a panel (an empty slot earns nothing), annual results at 25 to 100
        percent refill, and the contract rate that would match cash. Rows are payers,
        never clients, so no PHI is taken. New niche: nothing in the catalogue serves
        mental-health practices (nearest dental-ppo-writeoff-calculator). First
        visitor expected from "insurance vs private pay therapist" searches. Unverified
        on a real practice: tests use hand-calculated nets, an exact rate solve and
        no-network assertions. Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI
        workflow; refreshed the front-door mirror and tree counts.
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: market-garden-bed-planner
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built market-garden-bed-planner: a browser-local crop-mix
        planner for market gardens and small diversified farms. Enter one row per
        crop (yield per bed-foot, price, days in bed, cost, labor, what can be
        sold, a committed minimum) plus total bed-feet, season days and labor hours.
        It solves the plan that earns the most as an exact bounded-simplex linear
        program over bed-foot-days, labor hours and per-crop demand caps, and reads
        the dual prices off the same solution: what one more bed-foot, labor hour
        or 100 units of demand is worth, and the price rise that would bring each
        left-out crop in. It also prices a plan sorted by profit per bed-foot under
        the same limits (the folk method), re-solves with 10% more land or labor,
        and runs 400 seeded seasons with a shared-shock yield and price swing for a
        profit range. New niche after the e-commerce reorder, menu, agency, rent and
        podcast niches all hit existing ventures (0.42 to 0.85); duplicate_check.py
        best match here 0.21. First visitor expected from "which vegetables make the
        most money per bed foot" and "market garden crop profitability" searches and
        grower forums. Farm data never leaves the browser. Unverified on a working
        farm: tests include a hand-solved two-crop plan, strong duality, 200 random
        instances matched against exhaustive vertex enumeration, an optimizer-never-
        worse-than-sorted property over 100 random farms, and no-network assertions;
        a browser run loaded the example with no console errors and no axe violations.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: planning arithmetic on supplied figures, not advice, no warranty,
      independence from vendors stated, limits stated. Farm data never leaves the
      browser. Ethics: helps a small grower decide what to plant; nothing is sold,
      no data is collected and no referral is made.
  - venture: cottage-food-pricing-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built cottage-food-pricing-calculator: a browser-local tool
        for home bakers and cottage-food makers. Paste one row per product
        (ingredients per batch, units, minutes, packaging, current price); it
        computes the full cost per sellable unit including the maker's time,
        overhead and unsold goods, the price to charge online, at a farmers market
        (booth fee spread over units sold) and wholesale, with margin as a share of
        price and the card fee paid out of it, a store shelf price, and what the
        maker earns per hour at the current price. New niche: nothing in the
        catalogue prices homemade food. First visitor expected from "how to price
        baked goods" searches. Unverified on a real kitchen: tests use
        hand-calculated costs and prices and no-network assertions. Registered
        score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow; refreshed the
        front-door mirror and tree counts.
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: freelance-retainer-vs-hourly-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built freelance-retainer-vs-hourly-calculator: a browser-local tool that replays a proposed
        monthly retainer against a freelancer's own time log. Per client (at least six
        months, zero-filled gaps) it reports mean, median and 80th-percentile monthly
        hours with 300-resample seeded bootstrap ranges, the effective hourly rate at the
        median, 80th-percentile and worst month, break-even hours, the share of months
        where hourly would have paid more, the retainer that hits a target rate at a
        chosen coverage percentile, and a hold-out that calls the history unstable when
        average hours move more than 25%. duplicate_check.py best match 0.41
        (freelance-writer-rate-calculator); freelance-retainer-calculator prices from
        income-goal assumptions, not a log. First visitor expected from r/freelance,
        r/consulting and "retainer vs hourly pricing" searches. Unverified on real logs:
        tests use hand-counted months, a simulated uniform-hours client with a known
        80th percentile, a shift the hold-out must flag, and no-network assertions.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: payroll-tax-deposit-penalty-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built payroll-tax-deposit-penalty-calculator: a browser-local
        tool for small employers. Paste payday liabilities and deposits; it sets the
        schedule from the lookback total ($50,000 line), dates every deposit (the
        15th for monthly, Wednesday or Friday for semiweekly with the third-banking-day
        holiday rule, the $100,000 next-day rule and the monthly-to-semiweekly switch,
        a federal banking calendar computed from rules rather than a table), prices
        late deposits at the 2%, 5% and 10% tiers, and shows the penalty three ways:
        the IRS newest-liability-first default, oldest first, and the cheapest legal
        designation of the user's own deposits, solved as a min-cost transportation
        problem. Omits interest and the 15% post-notice tier and says so. New niche:
        duplicate_check.py best match 0.20 (rd-tax-credit-calculator, an unrelated
        credit); no Form 941 deposit tool exists in the catalogue. First visitor
        expected from "monthly or semiweekly depositor", "failure to deposit penalty
        calculator" and "941 deposit due dates" searches. Unverified by a tax
        professional: tests pin hand-counted holidays and due dates, tier boundaries,
        a worked designation example (default 1,040 vs designated 740), an optimality
        property check and no-network assertions. Registered score row, launch date,
        category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: home-care-agency-margin-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built home-care-agency-margin-calculator: a browser-local tool for non-medical
        home care agencies. Paste one row per payer (bill rate, billed hours a month,
        caregiver wage, share paid, days to payment, visit length, unpaid travel); it
        loads each wage with payroll tax, workers' comp, overtime and unbilled drive
        time, and computes cost, margin and margin percent per billed hour, the bill
        rate that reaches a target margin, the monthly cost of a one-dollar wage raise,
        receivables, and the break-even refill share for dropping a payer (an unfilled
        hour earns and costs nothing). Rows are payers, never clients or caregivers, so
        no PHI is taken. New niche: nothing in the catalogue serves home care (nearest
        employee-cost-calculator, staffing-markup-calculator). First visitor expected
        from "home care agency profit margin" searches. Unverified on a real agency:
        tests use hand-calculated costs, exact rate solves and no-network assertions.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow. A first draft
        of a towing venture was discarded after finding tow-motor-club-call-calculator
        already covers it (slug greps missed the short stem).
    mrr_end: 0
  - venture: family-child-care-time-space-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built family-child-care-time-space-calculator: a browser-local
        time-space percentage tool for home day care providers. Enter the rooms
        used (exclusive-use rooms count at full area, others scaled by hours),
        weekly care and prep hours, weeks open, days available and annual home
        expenses. It reports the time share over 24 x days available, the
        business-use share, each expense split into business and personal, a
        simplified-method comparison with the rate and cap as inputs, and what one
        more weekly hour is worth. New niche: childcare-tuition-calculator prices a
        classroom and home-office-deduction-calculator is generic; neither does the
        day-care hours-over-8,760 rule. First visitor expected from "time space
        percentage calculator daycare" searches in provider communities. No child
        or family data; nothing leaves the browser. Unverified on a filed return:
        tests use hand-calculated shares, exclusive and regular rooms, cap and
        validation cases and no-network assertions. Registered score row, launch
        date, category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not tax advice, no warranty,
      tax-year constants are inputs, limits stated. No child data. Ethics: helps a
      small provider compute a figure their preparer will check.
  - venture: adu-payback-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built adu-payback-calculator: a browser-local payback and
        return calculator for an accessory dwelling unit. Enter build cost lines
        with contingency, financing share, rate and term, rent with vacancy,
        management, owner-use months and growth, operating costs, hold period,
        value uplift and discount rate. It projects year-by-year cash flow and
        reports yield on cost, simple payback, equity IRR and NPV, the rent for
        NPV zero and for year-1 cash zero, and rent and build-cost sensitivity
        tables, with CSV export. New niche: duplicate_check.py top score 0.17, no
        venture covers ADUs. First visitor expected from "is an ADU worth it" and
        "ADU cost vs rental income" searches and r/ADU threads. Unverified on a
        real project: tests use hand-calculated amortisation, IRR/NPV and
        break-even cases and no-network assertions. Registered score row, launch
        date, category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not investment or construction
      advice, no warranty, no market data asserted, limits stated. Ethics: helps a
      homeowner see the numbers before a large spend.
  - venture: dog-grooming-profit-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built dog-grooming-profit-calculator: a browser-local tool for
        dog groomers. Enter services with price, minutes, supplies and dogs per
        week plus overhead; it reports profit per hour by service after card fees
        and overhead, the price that hits an hourly target, own shop versus booth
        rent versus commission on the same weekly mix, and the share of dogs a
        price raise can lose before it costs money. New niche: no grooming venture
        existed (duplicate_check.py closest 0.32, unrelated). First visitor expected
        from "how much to charge for dog grooming" and "booth rent vs commission dog
        groomer" searches and groomer communities. No client or pet data; nothing
        leaves the browser. Unverified on a real shop's books: tests use
        hand-calculated per-service, weekly, model and break-even cases. Registered
        score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow. Also published the
        stale gh-pages snapshot at session start (pages_state: current).
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not tax advice, no warranty,
      limits stated. No client data. Ethics: helps a small operator price honestly.
  - venture: massage-therapist-profit-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built massage-therapist-profit-calculator: a browser-local
        tool for massage therapists. Enter session types with price, minutes,
        supplies and sessions per week plus overhead and a no-show rate; it reports
        profit per hour by session after card fees, no-shows and overhead, the price
        that hits an hourly target (repriced for no-shows), own practice versus room
        rent versus employee split on the same weekly mix, and the share of clients
        a price raise can lose before it costs money. New niche: no massage venture
        existed (duplicate_check.py closest 0.27, unrelated). First visitor expected
        from "how much to charge for a massage" and "room rent vs commission
        massage" searches and therapist communities. No client or health data;
        nothing leaves the browser. Unverified on a real practice's books: tests use
        hand-calculated per-session, no-show, weekly, model and break-even cases.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not tax advice, no warranty,
      limits stated. No client or health data. Ethics: helps a small operator price
      honestly.
  - venture: dj-gig-profit-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built dj-gig-profit-calculator: a browser-local tool for
        mobile and wedding DJs. Enter packages with price, event hours, gig costs
        and gigs per month plus overhead; it reports profit per hour worked with
        setup, travel and planning counted, the price that hits an hourly target,
        direct clients versus a lead marketplace versus an agency subcontract on the
        same mix, and the share of gigs a price raise can lose before it costs
        money. New niche: no DJ venture existed (duplicate_check.py closest 0.38,
        adjacent event trades). First visitor expected from "how much to charge as a
        wedding DJ" searches and DJ communities. No client data; nothing leaves the
        browser. Unverified on a real DJ's books: tests use hand-calculated cases.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule, rate decision and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not tax advice, no warranty, limits
      stated. No client data. Ethics: helps a small operator price honestly.
  - venture: wedding-photographer-profit-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built wedding-photographer-profit-calculator: a browser-local
        tool for wedding and event photographers. Enter packages with price, coverage
        hours, job costs and jobs per month plus overhead; it counts travel, client
        time and culling and editing hours on every job and reports profit per hour
        worked beside the headline rate per coverage hour, the price that hits an
        hourly target, own clients versus a lead marketplace versus shooting for a
        studio, and the share of jobs a price raise can lose before it costs money.
        Niche check: duplicate_check.py closest 0.41 (photo-addon-pricing-calculator,
        one add-on rather than whole packages). First visitor expected from "how much
        to charge for wedding photography" searches. No client data; nothing leaves
        the browser. Unverified on a real photographer's books: tests use
        hand-calculated cases. Registered score row, launch date, category rule, rate
        decision and CI workflow.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, not tax advice, no warranty, limits
      stated. No client data. Ethics: helps a small operator price honestly.
  - venture: shipping-box-size-optimizer
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built shipping-box-size-optimizer: a browser-local tool for
        online sellers who pack their own orders. Enter products with packed size,
        weight and orders per month plus the cartons on offer; it solves which 1 to
        10 box sizes to stock (p-median: exact enumeration when small, multi-start
        Teitz-Bart swap search otherwise) counting dimensional weight, box cost and
        void fill, and reports the saving of each extra size, the box per product,
        and today's boxes against the best set, with optional custom-size
        candidates and a pasted rate card. New niche: duplicate_check.py closest
        parcel-dim-weight-calculator 0.17 (single carton, now cross-linked). First
        visitor expected from "what size shipping boxes should I stock" searches and
        seller forums. No customer data; nothing leaves the browser. Unverified on a
        real shop's invoices: tests use hand-calculated costs and check the local
        search against exhaustive enumeration. Registered score row, launch date,
        category rule, CI workflow and a guide page whose worked example is
        recomputed by the suite.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic and optimization on supplied figures, no carrier rates or
      box prices asserted, surcharges not priced and said so, no warranty. No
      customer data. Ethics: helps a small seller cut shipping waste.
  - venture: container-load-planner
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built container-load-planner: a browser-local 3D load planner
        for small exporters, Amazon/FBA and DTC sellers shipping cartons or pallets.
        Enter cargo lines (size, weight, quantity, rotation, highest layer, weight
        allowed on top), pick a 20 ft, 40 ft, 40 ft high cube, 53 ft trailer, box
        truck, pallet or custom size; an extreme-point packer with seeded restarts
        reports units packed and left over, volume and weight use, containers for the
        whole load (greedy, tail merged), to-scale top and side views, a loading list
        and a loose-versus-pallets comparison across every standard size, metric or
        imperial. New niche: duplicate_check.py closest amazon-fba-calculator 0.20
        (fees, not loading); shipping-box-size-optimizer is its cross-linked
        neighbour. First visitor expected from "how many pallets fit in a 40ft
        container" searches. No cargo data leaves the browser. Unverified on a real
        loading: tests use hand-computed fits and random loads checked by an
        independent verifier for overlap, bounds, payload, rotation, support and
        stacking. Registered score row, launch date, category rule, CI workflow and a
        guide page whose worked example is recomputed by the suite.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic and a packing heuristic on supplied figures, a planning
      aid and not a load-securing, axle-weight or legal certificate, no freight rates
      asserted, nominal container sizes labelled and editable, no warranty. No cargo
      data. Ethics: helps a small shipper avoid over-booking space.
  - venture: production-mix-optimizer
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built production-mix-optimizer: a browser-local tool for
        bakeries, workshops and small makers. Enter products (price, unit cost,
        minimum, maximum, batch size) and limited resources (oven, machine, labour
        hours, optional overtime); a two-phase simplex with branch and bound on whole
        batches finds the most profitable weekly mix, then reports the shadow price of
        each bottleneck and how far it holds, each product's resource cost and net per
        unit, and the plan against two rule-of-thumb plans, with a CSV. New niche
        after a first idea (container-load-planner) was merged by another session
        minutes earlier (#6146); duplicate_check.py closest cnc-machining-quote-calculator
        0.38 (generic word overlap, quotes one job). First visitor expected from "product
        mix optimization" and "is overtime worth it" searches. No customer data; nothing
        leaves the browser. Unverified on a real business: tests use hand-solved problems,
        brute-force comparison, a cycling-prone degenerate LP, duality checks and a guide
        worked example the suite recomputes. Registered score row, launch date, category
        rule, CI workflow and publish-surface row.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, no prices, costs or capacities
      asserted, no warranty. No customer data. Ethics: helps a small maker use scarce
      hours well.
  - venture: crypto-cost-basis-calculator
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built crypto-cost-basis-calculator: a browser-local lot matcher
        for people who bought or earned crypto at several prices. Paste or open a CSV
        of buys, sales and income (exchange-style headers recognised); it matches each
        sale to purchase lots under FIFO, LIFO, HIFO, LOFO or a tax-aware greedy rule,
        splits sales into short-term and long-term rows by holding period, optionally
        matches wallet by wallet, compares all five methods on the chosen year with an
        estimated tax, lists coins and basis still held, and exports Form 8949 style
        rows. New niche: duplicate_check.py closest like-kind-exchange-1031-calculator
        0.18. First visitor expected from "crypto FIFO vs HIFO" and "Form 8949 crypto
        csv" searches and r/CryptoTax threads in filing season. No customer data;
        nothing leaves the browser. Unverified on a real return: tests use hand-computed
        FIFO/LIFO/HIFO figures plus quantity and basis conservation checks across all
        methods on seeded random books. Registered score row, launch date, category
        rule, CI workflow and a guide page whose worked example is recomputed by the
        suite.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic on supplied figures, no prices fetched, no claim about
      which lot method a filer may use, omissions stated, no warranty. No customer
      data. Ethics: helps people compute their own gains privately.
  - venture: rental-fleet-size-optimizer
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built rental-fleet-size-optimizer: a browser-local tool for
        businesses that rent out identical units (tents, kayaks, scaffold, camera
        gear, tool kits). Enter seasons of demand, rental lengths, price, cost per
        rental and the yearly cost of owning a unit; it computes the yearly profit of
        every fleet size two ways, the Erlang loss formula per season and a seeded
        day-by-day simulation (Poisson or negative-binomial requests, common random
        numbers across fleet sizes), and recommends how many units to own with turn-away
        rates, a bad year (10th percentile), the days the marginal unit adds against
        the days it needs to pay for itself, an optional turn-away cap and its cost, a
        comparison with today's fleet, and how the answer moves with demand. New niche:
        duplicate_check.py closest equipment-rental-break-even 0.18 (one machine's
        break-even, not how many to own). First visitor expected from "how many units
        should my rental business own" searches. No customer data; nothing leaves the
        browser. Unverified on a real business's books: tests check Erlang B against
        its closed form, the simulation against the exact day-batch formula for
        one-day rentals, and the guide's worked example is recomputed by the suite.
        Registered score row, launch date, category rule, CI workflow and a guide page.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic and simulation on supplied figures, not tax, financial or
      business advice, no demand, price or asset cost asserted, no warranty, limits
      stated. No customer data. Ethics: helps a small rental owner avoid buying units
      that never pay for themselves.
  - venture: tile-layout-planner
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built tile-layout-planner: a browser-local tile layout planner
        for installers and DIY. Enter a room, cut-outs and a tile (straight, running
        bond or diagonal); exact polygon clipping lays out the real tiles, a search
        over grid offsets and tile direction finds the layout with the fewest cuts
        thinner than the user's limit then the fewest tiles, a greedy guillotine plan
        reuses offcuts, and the page shows a to-scale plan, cut list, tiles and boxes
        to order and a corner / centred / best comparison, metric or imperial. New
        niche: duplicate_check.py closest flooring-bid-calculator 0.35 (prices a job,
        no layout). First visitor expected from "how many tiles do I need" searches.
        No room data leaves the browser. Unverified on a real floor: tests use
        hand-computed layouts and random rooms whose pieces must add up to the floor
        (exactly, with no grout). Registered score row, launch date, category rule, CI
        workflow and a guide page whose worked example is recomputed by the suite.
    mrr_end: 0
    gates:
      liability_containment: pass
      ethical_robustness: pass
    gate_note: >-
      Liability: arithmetic and geometry on supplied figures, a planning aid and not
      installation instructions or a material guarantee, no tile price asserted, no
      warranty. No customer data. Ethics: helps a homeowner or installer avoid
      over-buying and bad cuts.
  - venture: event-seating-chart-optimizer
    agent_spend_usd: null
    human_hours: 0
    outcomes:
      - >-
        Graduated and built event-seating-chart-optimizer: a browser-local seating chart
        optimizer for weddings, banquets and events. Paste a guest list (optional family
        or party per guest), write wishes as text (+ together, ++ really together, !
        apart, !! never, @ pin to a table); simulated annealing with a softened
        never-together penalty plus a hill-climbing polish assigns every guest to a table
        within capacity, with tables filled evenly by default. Shows each table, every
        unmet wish and split family, a comparison with seating in list order, and a CSV
